      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-216",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t+3{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+6t+12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+6t+12{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6+24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =6+24(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$.",
